1
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:11,750
I'm traveling through a tunnel right now on a train that's going 200 kilometers an hour.

2
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:17,890
And above me, there's two and a half kilometers of pure rock.

3
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:21,550
That's a mile and a half of nothing but mountain.

4
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:25,420
This tunnel is 57 kilometers long.

5
00:00:25,420 --> 00:00:26,530
It's 35 miles.

6
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:28,630
It's the longest on the planet.

7
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:38,320
A few months ago,

8
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:39,080
I asked the people

9
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,320
who run Switzerland's trains

10
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:42,620
if they would let me spend a week doing nothing

11
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,340
And in this moment,

12
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:02,260
I'm in the middle of a race to see

13
00:01:02,260 --> 00:01:05,420
if I can step foot on all 26 Swiss regions,

14
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:10,650
or cantons, in under 24 hours, but only using public transportation.

15
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:19,740
And along the way,

16
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:24,260
locals who responded to my call for stories on our community -driven journalism platform

17
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:26,170
are going to help me on this challenge.

18
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,270
We have a new plan.

19
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:35,030
I'm an American who doesn't really understand trains, I'm embarrassed to say.

20
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:37,910
My country is a country that loves cars.

21
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:40,840
So I'm here to try to understand what they've built,

22
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:41,720
how it works,

23
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:42,570
how it's designed,

24
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:44,820
what are the crazy engineering feats

25
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:46,710
that they've done to make this system work,

26
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:52,690
and most importantly, what can we, outside of this country, learn from it all.

27
00:02:01,780 --> 00:02:03,850
Before my big speed run through the country,

28
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:06,020
my first item of business is to see

29
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:09,530
if Swiss engineering is as extreme and rugged as I've heard.

30
00:42:14,580 --> 00:42:16,840
Luckily, I booked a hotel up the hill.

31
00:42:16,840 --> 00:42:17,700
I'm gonna go walk to it

32
00:42:17,700 --> 00:42:17,900
and and see

33
00:42:17,900 --> 00:42:19,730
if they'll let me in, even though it's almost two in the morning.

34
00:42:21,900 --> 00:42:25,110
And with that, good night.
